{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: the owned fresh client is never closed on this path**

`sendProviderFetch(client ?? http.Client(), request, …)` — when no client is injected, the freshly created `http.Client()` leaks (pre-existing, but this PR touches exactly this line and the sibling `chatgpt_oauth._tokenRequest` demonstrates the established pattern):

```dart
final httpClient = client ?? http.Client();
final ownsClient = client == null;
…
} finally {
  if (ownsClient) httpClient.close();
}
```

This now matters more than before the PR: on a read-leg timeout the response body is abandoned mid-flight (see the `sendProviderFetch` ceiling), and an unclosed client keeps that socket alive until GC instead of releasing it. Adopting the same `ownsClient`/`finally`-close here makes the timeout path self-cleaning for the aiin endpoints the issue was filed against.
